      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-170004",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n${x - 2y = 3; 3x - 4y = 7$\n\nThe variable $x$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1. Multiply the first equation by $-3$ and obtain\n$-3x + 6y =-9$.\n2. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n$\u22ef?\u22ef =-2$.\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(x, y)$ of the system."
    },
