      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-52139",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n${12v - 32w =-8; - 2v + 6w = 2$\n\nThe variable $v$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1. Multiply the second equation by $6$ and obtain\n$-12v + 36w|= 12$.\n2. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n$\u22ef?\u22ef = 4$.\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(v, w)$ of the system."
